## Tip Amounts by Price: $20 to $200 Pedicures

How much should you tip for a $45 pedicure? Between $6.75 and $9, with $9 as the more generous end for solid service. Working out <strong>how much to tip for a pedicure</strong> at any price comes down to the same 15-20% split, and the table below saves the arithmetic across every common tier.

- **$20 pedicure:** $3 to $4
- **$30 pedicure:** $4.50 to $6
- **$40 pedicure:** $6 to $8
- **$50 pedicure:** $7.50 to $10
- **$60 pedicure:** $9 to $12
- **$70 pedicure:** $10.50 to $14
- **$100 pedicure:** $15 to $20
- **$150 pedicure:** $22.50 to $30
- **$200 pedicure:** $30 to $40

Is $5 okay for a tip on a pedicure? On anything under roughly $30, yes, it lands right inside the 15-20% window and is a completely reasonable tip. The reassurance people are searching for at this end of the scale is real: a small dollar figure can look stingy sitting on the counter even when the percentage behind it is exactly right. A five dollar tip on a $25 pedicure is 20%, full stop.

Was a 25% tip okay on a $40 pedicure? More than okay, that is $10, sitting above standard as a genuine thank you for service that went beyond routine, not a number that needs justifying afterward.

The top of the range works the same way. A $200 pedicure, the kind found at a resort spa or during a deluxe multi-step treatment, still follows the same 15-20% math. That is $30 to $40, a larger figure in isolation but proportionally identical to the $6 tip on a $30 visit. For how these price tiers map to the type of pedicure and salon behind them, <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/nail-costs/pedicure-cost'>see exact pedicure price tiers by type and salon</a> for the full cost breakdown by service level.

