**How much do you tip for a $30 pedicure?** Between $4.50 and $6, calculated at the standard 15-20% range.

**How much do you tip for a $100 pedicure?** Between $15 and $20, with $20 as the safer default for solid, unremarkable service.

**Do you tip on the discounted price or the original price?** Always the original price. A coupon or gift card changes what was paid, not what the technician's time was worth.

**Is 20% a good tip for a pedicure?** Yes, it is the most commonly cited standard across salons and the number to default to when unsure.

**How much do I tip if I pay by credit card instead of cash?** The same percentage applies either way. Cash simply reaches the technician faster and avoids processing fees, which is why it remains the preferred method when available.

Independent financial guidance lines up with this same floor. NerdWallet's own reporting places nail salon gratuity in the 10-20% range, which sits comfortably inside the standard this guide uses throughout. When in doubt, 20% resolves nearly every version of this question standing at a register.

